==Trivia==
*The 魂底 in Depths of My Heart's Japanese name (魂底からの帰化, ''Kontei Kara no Kika'', "Naturalization from the Bottom of the Soul") is not an actual word. It consists of the kanji for "soul" (魂) and "bottom" (底) and shares its pronunciation with 根底 ''kontei'' (the basis or foundation of something), whose first kanji (根) instead means a plant's root, the source or root of something, the cause or basis for something, or the nature one has from birth.

